{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Report\n\nMultiple concurrent sessions simultaneously report `rebar review-plan` returning **INDETERMINATE** (unsigned, no determinate PASS/FAIL verdict). Sudden fleet-wide onset during heavy concurrent multi-worktree activity (~70 worktrees; multiple sessions + a fanned-out batch of debug agents each running review-plan).\n\n## Observed\n\n- INDETERMINATE affects MULTIPLE independent sessions at once (systemic, not per-ticket).\n- Local host HEALTHY: load ~3.5, disk 28%, no orphaned busy-loops. NOT local exhaustion.\n- Provider config: rebar DEFAULTS TO AWS BEDROCK (`[llm] model = bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8`, acct 896586841071/us-east-1). The frontier class (review-plan) is `frontier = { model = \"bedrock:opus\", fallback = [{ model = \"anthropic:opus\" }] }`.\n- Tickets branch shows three-way divergence — heavy concurrent ticket writes.\n\n## Proven root cause (Phase 1 — H1 wins; two coupled defects)\n\nUnder concurrent multi-session load the SHARED Bedrock account throttles at the ACCOUNT level. The failure chain:\n\n1. `bedrock:opus` throttled → botocore adaptive retry exhausts → `ModelHTTPError(429)` → classifies `WAIT_AND_RETRY` (retryable).\n2. `should_fall_back(429)` = True → the chain moves to the `anthropic:opus` fallback.\n3. The fallback is KEYLESS (`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` absent) → instant `TypeError: Could not resolve authentication method`. `should_fall_back(TypeError)` = False, so pydantic-ai's `FallbackModel` **bare-reraises that terminal `TypeError` alone and DISCARDS the primary's retained retryable 429** (it only bundles a `FallbackExceptionGroup` when the LAST leg's predicate is True).\n4. `classify_llm_failure(TypeError)` → `NEEDS_INVESTIGATION` (non-retryable) → the gate emits a hard **INDETERMINATE** instead of the retryable **exit-11**.\n\nShared account ⇒ fleet-wide simultaneity. There is a LATENT SECOND BUG behind the first: even if a `FallbackExceptionGroup` WERE produced, `failure._map` classified it with a blanket `CHANGE_PROVIDER_OR_MODEL` (non-retryable), ignoring the leg dispositions — so the retryable primary would still be masked. Both defects must be fixed for the chain to preserve a retryable terminal. (Full runtime proof + H2 stale-store rejection in the Phase-1 RCA comment.)\n\n## Fix plan (Phase 2 — disposition-preserving fallback chain, operator-approved)\n\nBehavior: try the PRIMARY (exhaust its retries), then the fallback(s) (exhaust theirs), then if the terminal condition ACROSS THE WHOLE CHAIN is retryable, FAIL RETRYABLE (exit-11), never a hard INDETERMINATE. The fallback stays fully eligible — the fix only stops a fallback leg's non-retryable failure from MASKING a retryable primary failure. Two changes, both on existing seams in `src/rebar/llm/`, at the SHARED classification/construction core so all gate surfaces inherit them once:\n\n**Change 1 — exhaust into a `FallbackExceptionGroup`, never bare-reraise a fallback leg** (`model_classes.py`). Make `should_fall_back` leg-aware: a NON-PRIMARY leg's failure is always retained (returns True) so the chain bundles every leg — including the primary's retained 429 — into the group at exhaustion, instead of pydantic-ai bare-reraising the terminal leg alone. Each non-primary candidate is tagged in `build_fallback_model` via a small `_wrap_fallback_leg` `WrapperModel`. The PRIMARY leg keeps the deliberately NARROW guard unchanged — a credential/size/quota error still fails LOUD and is never masked by shopping for a working key. (The credential-masking guard is about failing over FROM a primary credential error; here the credential failure is on the LAST leg with nowhere further to go, so the requirement is only that the terminal failure retains the group.)\n\n**Change 2 — classify a group by its MOST-RECOVERABLE leg** (`failure.py`). Replace the blanket `FallbackExceptionGroup → CHANGE_PROVIDER_OR_MODEL` arm in `_map` with `_classify_fallback_group`: iterate the group's legs, classify each through the TOTAL public classifier, and return the most-recoverable (a retryable `WAIT_AND_RETRY`/`RETRY_NOW` on ANY leg wins). A group whose legs are ALL genuinely non-retryable keeps `CHANGE_PROVIDER_OR_MODEL` (the whole chain is unavailable — switching model/provider is what would address it). Classifier stays total.\n\nTogether: throttle → group retains [429, TypeError] → classified `WAIT_AND_RETRY` → exit-11 retryable. `_RETRYABLE` in `failure.py` is UNCHANGED. The primary predicate contract is UNCHANGED, so the existing predicate/e2e failover tests and the `rebar.toml`/docs comments about the availability classes stay accurate.\n\n**Scope (3 files — enumerated for the plan-review out-of-artifact-consumer check):**\n- `src/rebar/llm/failure.py` — Change 2: `_GROUP_RECOVERABILITY` + `_classify_fallback_group`; the `_map` group arm calls it.\n- `src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py` — Change 1: leg-aware `should_fall_back` (early retain-marker check + two-rule docstring), `_FALLBACK_LEG_ATTR`, `_fallback_leg_wrapper_class`, `_tag_fallback_leg`, `_wrap_fallback_leg`, and the non-primary wrap in `build_fallback_model`.\n- `tests/unit/test_throttle_no_failover_1c0d.py` — NEW held-out oracle (see Testing).\n\n**Attribution:** caused_by `8fbd-e9d5-326e-40d8` (commit `6d4f394195b2`, \"Enable class-scoped Anthropic fallback\", 2026-08-10), class `plan_defect`. Both latent defects (the leg-agnostic `should_fall_back`, `72e59d982fee` 2026-07-31; the blanket group arm, `4291b9a5600e` 2026-07-09) PREDATE 8fbd, which merely ENABLED the anthropic fallback in `rebar.toml` — activating both. Fix site ≠ cause site.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] End-to-end (mocked provider, NO real Bedrock): a throttled `ModelHTTPError(429)` primary in a real `FallbackModel` (built through `build_fallback_model`) behind a keyless `anthropic:opus` fallback surfaces as the **exit-11 retryable** disposition (`WAIT_AND_RETRY`), NOT INDETERMINATE. Proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_throttle_no_failover_1c0d.py`.\n- [ ] A `FallbackExceptionGroup` bundling [retryable 429, non-retryable TypeError] classifies as the **retryable** class, independent of leg order. Same module.\n- [ ] An all-non-retryable group stays `CHANGE_PROVIDER_OR_MODEL` (over-broadening guard). Same module; the pre-existing `test_llm_failure_classifier.py` group case still passes.\n- [ ] The PRIMARY-leg failover contract is UNCHANGED: the existing `tests/unit/test_llm_fallback_chain.py` predicate/e2e suite stays GREEN without edits (529 fails over, 401 does not).\n- [ ] A RED oracle fails before the change and passes after; two mutations (revert Change 2 → group test RED; revert Change 1 → e2e RED reproducing the exact keyless-auth `TypeError` INDETERMINATE) are caught under `sandbox-exec`.\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` clean; no new dependency; no test weakening.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `pytest tests/unit/test_throttle_no_failover_1c0d.py` — the held-out RED oracle: the keyless-fallback-after-throttle e2e (exit-11 retryable), the direct group classifier (most-recoverable leg, order-independent), and the all-non-retryable over-broadening guard.\n- `pytest tests/unit/test_llm_fallback_chain.py tests/unit/test_llm_failure_classifier.py` — the pre-existing predicate/failover + classifier suites stay GREEN unchanged (primary contract preserved).\n- `make lint` and `make typecheck` — clean.\n- Mutation-with-teeth inside `sandbox-exec -f` (no `timeout` binary on this host): (a) revert Change 2 to the blanket `CHANGE_PROVIDER_OR_MODEL` → group test RED; (b) revert Change 1 so the chain bare-reraises → e2e RED reproducing the exact INDETERMINATE signature; restore → GREEN.\n\n## Investigate/repair WITHOUT adding Bedrock load\n\nDo NOT reproduce by running live review-plan storms against Bedrock. The classification path is reproduced entirely locally with an injected/mocked provider throttle. Reported against origin/main at commit 55589c15."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788053969070785482,"uuid":"f2c58aa2-1058-4779-a841-677b24e867a2"}